    "narrative":  {
                      "overview":  "Pizarra is a Spanish drawing tool inside Deska. Its approved direction is a compact, Excalidraw-like editor: the canvas fills the panel, the drawing tools float above it, and settings appear when relevant. The document is the visual focus.",
                      "dos":  [
                                  "Do preserve the full canvas, floating toolbar, and contextual left settings.",
                                  "Do use Deska tokens for interface chrome and keep board preferences separate.",
                                  "Do keep Spanish labels, visible keyboard focus, and programmatic control state.",
                                  "Do preserve existing drawing content and storage behavior during visual changes."
                              ],
                      "donts":  [
                                    "Don\u0027t add website navigation, hero sections, dashboard cards, or promotional content to this panel.",
                                    "Don\u0027t substitute a permanent sidebar for the contextual floating surfaces.",
                                    "Don\u0027t treat screenshots or synthetic test drawings as default user content.",
                                    "Don\u0027t invent new brand colors, fonts, decorative motion, or a product identity for this scoped editor."
                                ],
                      "keyCharacteristics":  [
                                                 "Selection, rectangle, diamond, ellipse, arrow, line, and text remain visible in the primary toolbar row. A trailing chevron reveals a secondary row for pen, eraser, fill, and sticky note.",
                                                 "The extra row closes on tool selection, Escape, or an outside click. Text stays directly available in the primary row.",
                                                 "Hand uses a compact tool button (32px) beside undo/redo, separated by a thin divider. Hand mode lasts for one drag, then restores the previously selected tool.",
